{"id": "EUVD-2026-76496", "enisaUuid": "9af7601f-c9aa-3cb9-86aa-43261e884830", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblock: validate user space vectors during extraction\n\nThe bio-based drivers don't necessarily check the alignment split, and\nstacking block drivers don't always handle a misalignment detected after\nsubmitting the bio. Validate user vectors against the device's\ndma_alignment as the bio is built from the iov_iter, rejecting\nmisaligned early with -EINVAL.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:17", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d44a97a3b1c00cc571245124e23e5ceb0a0225a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14b007e178811db72fbb1ebb3535160db6ec1e6a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rh46-v7ch-v9qg", "CVE-2026-89584"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "198c8e0b-4d55-3d3d-9485-150f71d30698", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1e22fc7b-669e-33eb-8c1c-b0395d53623e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "32ab60c8-9a35-3f96-bcf8-b5f1f78a1821", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "8f9a4e5c-2492-3479-a222-df0e025997d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ff3f74e145adc79b49668adb8de276446acf6be <d44a97a3b1c00cc571245124e23e5ceb0a0225a0"}, {"id": "c713dc8e-a5b4-32fb-b2f2-7abd36592435", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ec87f2f9-e66e-3299-9353-5eec5ce1e19b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ff3f74e145adc79b49668adb8de276446acf6be <14b007e178811db72fbb1ebb3535160db6ec1e6a"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "